  {
   "id": 1,
   "plugin": "Core",
   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "EMOTION\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: MIDI channel 5, CC 33 to 48\n   1 Strength of the feeling\n   2 How they move\n   3 Feeling in the voice\n   4 Amount of movement\n   5 Amount said\n   6 Posture changes\n   7 Size of the actions\n   8 Mood of the place\n   9 Mood of the light\n  10 Against the last scene\n  11 Feeling gap between characters\n  12 Mixed feelings\n  13 Said against meant\n  14 The eyes\n  15 The hands\n  16 Personal space\nCV-CC 2: MIDI channel 5, CC 49 to 64\n   1 Release\n   2 What the audience feels\n   3 suite: Feels loving\n   4 suite: Feels joyful\n   5 suite: Feels curious\n   6 suite: Feels melancholy\n   7 suite: Feels anxious\n   8 suite: Feels fearful\n   9 suite: Feels angry\n  10 suite: Feels triumphant\n  11 suite: Feels absurd\n  12 suite: Feels dreamlike\n  13 suite: Emotion lens\n  14 suite: Feeling of the scene\n  15 suite: Held-back tears\n  16 suite: Rage boils over\nCV-CC 3: MIDI channel 5, CC 65 to 80\n   1 suite: Quiet joy\n   2 suite: Frozen fear\n   3 suite: Mood whiplash\n   4 suite: Calm in the storm\n   5 suite: The mask slips\n   6 suite: Laughing through tears\n   7 suite: Brave face\n   8 suite: Dawning realization\n   9 suite: The breakdown\n  10 suite: Cold fury\n  11 suite: Giddy relief\n  12 suite: Numb shock\n  13 suite: Awkward tenderness\n  14 suite: Dread: we know, they don't\n  15 pair: When the mood of the light drops, the strength of the feeling rises\n  16 pair: When the feeling grows stronger, the posture changes more often\nCV-CC 4: MIDI channel 5, CC 81 to 96\n   1 pair: When a scene feels the opposite of the last one, the color shifts too\n   2 pair: When a feeling rises, the face shows it before the words\n   3 pair: When anger rises, the voice gets louder\n   4 pair: When fear rises, movement stops\n   5 pair: When one character's feeling overflows, others catch it\n   6 pair: When joy rises, the light warms\n   7 pair: When a trigger appears, the feeling turns\n   8 pair: After a release, the character is lighter\n   9 pair: When said and meant pull apart, the pauses grow\n  10 pair: When people move closer, the feeling grows\n  11 pair: When tears well, the shot gets closer\n  12 pair: When we know more than they do, tension rises\n  13 pair: When feelings mix, the face flickers\n  14 pairs: The body tells first\n  15 pairs: Feelings spread\n  16 pairs: What isn't said\nCV-CC 5: MIDI channel 5, CC 97 to 97\n   1 pairs: Closeness and dread"
   },
